tars.githubusercontent.com/u/63526047?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM","html_url":"https://github.com/sselecirPyM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sselecirPyM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T17:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T17:42:05Z","body":"> This feels like fake bindless. I don't think the \"big number\" approach is the way to go about it. This also has the problem of leaving descriptors uninitialized, which is illegal without the `VK_DESCRIPTOR_BINDING_PARTIALLY_BOUND_BIT` flag.\r\n> \r\n> For now, I think it would make more sense if you manually specified the upper array bounds in your GLSL, and filled the unused space with a \"default\" buffer. For that, we do need the support for multiple storage buffers from here.\r\n\r\nThe VK_DESCRIPTOR_BINDING_PARTIALLY_BOUND_BIT flag was added when creating the DescriptorSetLayout. And it is applied only in the ray tracing stage.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4025603206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4060763754","html_url":"https://github.com/godoten